{number: 146}
{title: O the Help that God has Given}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
O the [C] help that God has given
To His [F] children on the [C] way,
Leading from earth's shadowy paths
To [G7] everlasting [C] day!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C] Trust Him, trust Him,
He will never [F] leave thee nor for-[C] sake;
Trust Him, trust Him,
[G7] Every promise [C] keep.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
O the [C] love of God our Savior,
Reaching [F] downward to the [C] lost,
Lifting souls from sin and ruin,
[G7] Paid for at so great a [C] cost!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
O the [C] grace that never faileth,
Flowing [F] freely from a-[C] bove,
Filling every hungry spirit
[G7] With the fullness of His [C] love!
{end_of_verse}
